        "summary": "On a marketing site, every page except the home opens on a compact product header band: a title-size heading, one sticker, no actions. Plan prices are 18px flags inside cards. The reference treats its own pricing and features pages as posters. Each gets a full band hero with a display headline and several cropped stickers around it. On pricing, a black seam then closes that hero into a split band where each half holds one huge fee figure. So the page that sells the product, and its states, lose the system's loudest moment and read like a settings page.",
